    },
    {
      "page_idx": 3,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.079,
            0.025,
            0.572,
            0.079
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Reasons for Dramatic Progress"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.07,
            0.091,
            0.317,
            0.131
          ],
          "content": "**--- series of events**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.07,
            0.15,
            0.873,
            0.305
          ],
          "content": "**--- main on**<strong><u>e: machine perception is starting to work (f</u></strong>**inally!)** <strong><u>systems are starting to “hear” and “see”</u></strong> **after “only” 50+ yrs or research…**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.07,
            0.319,
            0.908,
            0.606
          ],
          "content": "**--- dramatic change: lots of AI techniques (reasoning, search, reinforcement learning, planning, decision theoretic methods) were developed assuming perceptual inputs were “somehow” provided to the system. But, e.g., robots could not really see or hear anything…**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.119,
            0.618,
            0.914,
            0.726
          ],
          "content": "**(e.g. 2005 Stanley car drove around “blind”, Thrun) Now, we can use output from a perceptual system and**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.218,
            0.739,
            0.865,
            0.786
          ],
          "content": "**leverage a broad range of existing AI techniques.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.12,
            0.797,
            0.927,
            0.846
          ],
          "content": "**Our systems are finally becoming “grounded in (our) world.”**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.221,
            0.857,
            0.979,
            0.967
          ],
          "content": "**Already: super-human face recognition (Facebook) super-human traffic sign recognition (Nvidia)**"
        }
      ]
    },
